 },
 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:08:24.597712Z",
 "text": "Under the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006* (RTA), this clause is not enforceable. \n\nUnder **section 20(1)** of the Act, the landlord is legally responsible for maintaining the rental unit in a good state of repair and fit for habitation, regardless of the cause of the non-repair. While a tenant can be held responsible for undue damage caused by wilful or negligent conduct (section 34), a clause shifting the landlord's statutory maintenance obligations entirely to the tenant directly conflicts with the Act. Pursuant to **section 4(1)**, any provision in a tenancy agreement that is inconsistent with the Act is void.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 20",
